Yes — exactly that. The whole design rests on it.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
`migrateShadowBranchIfNeeded` currently only knows "did HEAD move?" We're teaching it one additional question: "does HEAD's commit message carry *our session's* `LastCheckpointID` as an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer?" That one extra read turns a dumb HEAD-tracker into a reset-aware reconciler, and everything else (every hook callsite, the passive-status change, the orphan-shadow behavior) follows from it automatically.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

Concretely, inside `migrateShadowBranchIfNeeded` in `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_migration.go`:

```go
func (s *ManualCommitStrategy) migrateShadowBranchIfNeeded(ctx, repo, state) (bool, error) {
    // unchanged guard
    if state == nil || state.BaseCommit == "" {
        return false, nil
    }

    head, err := repo.Head()
    if err != nil { ... }
    currentHead := head.Hash().String()
    if state.BaseCommit == currentHead {
        return false, nil
    }

    // NEW: reconcile branch — read LastCheckpointID from state, parse HEAD's
    // commit message, check if any Entire-Checkpoint trailer matches.
    if !state.LastCheckpointID.IsEmpty() {
        commit, err := repo.CommitObject(head.Hash())
        if err == nil {
            for _, cp := range trailers.ParseAllCheckpoints(commit.Message) {
                if cp.String() == state.LastCheckpointID.String() {
                    state.BaseCommit = currentHead
                    state.AttributionBaseCommit = currentHead
                    logging.Info(..., "reconciled session to known checkpoint on HEAD")
                    return true, nil
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // existing migrate path: rename shadow branch, update BaseCommit only
    ...
}
```

That's the whole addition — one new lookup block before the existing migration logic. Callers don't change (SaveStep / SaveTaskStep / UserPromptSubmit already invoke it). Status strips its mutation and becomes a pure reporter.

